  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The photographs are antique shop finds as well as one download from the Library of Congress photographs on line. They date between 1915 and 1935. All required extensive clean-up in Photoshop. The grayscale images were converted to tritones using Pantones 363, 200 and Yellow. They were converted to RGB for printing on an Epson C88+. The Virginia map on the back of the concertina was scanned from another antique shop atlas from the same period as the diary"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hedi Kyle's flag book structure, attached to illustrated paper over boards on either side. Paper is Cougar Opaque 80# cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Typefaces used are FF Mister K for the script and Borutta Group's Adagio Serif for the colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
